"Prise en charge des laboratoires de développement à domicile","Utilisation de l''interface de ligne de commande (CLI) pour configurer les projets"],"de":["Einrichtung von Projekten mit KI-Agenten","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Node.js","Automatisierung von Entwicklungsaufgaben","Unterstützung von Entwicklungslabors zu Hause","Verwendung der Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI) zur Konfiguration von Projekten"],"pt":["Configuração de projetos de home lab com ferramentas de IA","Integração com React, Python e Node.js","Suporte a CLI para automação de tarefas","Arquivos de exemplo para ajudar a começar","Documentação detalhada para facilitar a configuração"],"ru":["Настройка домашних лабораторных проектов с ИИ Агентами","Интеграция с React, Python и Node.js","Поддержка CLI для автоматизации задач","Примерные файлы для помощи в начале работы","Дetailed документация для облегчения настройки"],"ar":["إعداد مشاريع مختبر المنزل مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع React و Python و Node.js","دعم CLI للتحكم الآلي في المهام","ملفات مثال لمساعدتك في البدء","توثيق مفصل لتسهيل الإعداد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用 setup-project","什么是 AI 智能代理","setup-project 安装指南","setup-project 替代品","setup-project 教程","home lab 环境搭建","AI 智能代理工具","开发效率提升"],"ja":["setup-project の使い方","AI エージェントとは","setup-project インストール ガイド","setup-project の代替","setup-project チュートリアル","home lab 環境の構築","AI エージェント ツール","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["setup-project 사용 방법","AI 에이전트란","setup-project 설치 가이드","setup-project 대체품","setup-project 튜토리얼","홈 랩 환경 구축","AI 에이전트 도구","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["cómo usar Agentes de IA","qué es un Agente de IA","alternativas a Agentes de IA","Agentes de IA vs herramientas de desarrollo","instalación de Agentes de IA","guía de configuración de Agentes de IA","desarrollo de proyectos con Agentes de IA","herramientas de desarrollo para laboratorios de casa"],"fr":["comment utiliser des Outils d''IA","qu''est-ce qu''un Outil d''IA","alternatives aux Outils d''IA","Outils d''IA vs outils de développement","installation d''Outils d''IA","guide de configuration d''Outils d''IA","développement de projets avec des Outils d''IA","outils de développement pour laboratoires à domicile"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu KI-Agenten","KI-Agenten vs Entwicklungstools","Installation von KI-Agenten","Anleitung zur Konfiguration von KI-Agenten","Entwicklung von Projekten mit KI-Agenten","Entwicklungstools für Heimlabore"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de IA","o que é setup-project","ferramentas de IA para home lab","setup-project vs outros agentes","instalar setup-project","guia de configuração do setup-project","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","setup-project para iniciantes"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое setup-project","ИИ Агенты для домашнего лабораторного проекта","setup-project vs другие агенты","установить setup-project","руководство по настройке setup-project","ИИ Агенты для разработчиков","setup-project для начинающих"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هو setup-project","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لمشاريع مختبر المنزل","setup-project مقابل أدوات أخرى","تثبيت setup-project","دليل إعداد setup-project","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","setup-project للمبتدئين"]}},"owner":"ViktorBarzin","repo":"infra","repoPath":"ViktorBarzin/infra","stars":4,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-26T21:21:50Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"setup-project","description":"|","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Setup Project Skill\n\n**Purpose**: Deploy a new self-hosted service to the Kubernetes cluster from a GitHub repository.\n\n**When to use**: User provides a GitHub URL or project name and wants to deploy it to the cluster.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Research Phase\n\n**Input**: GitHub repository URL or project name\n\n**Actions**:\n- Visit the GitHub repository\n- Check the README for:\n  - Official Docker image (Docker Hub, ghcr.io, etc.)\n  - docker-compose.yml file\n  - Self-hosting documentation\n  - Required","body":"# Setup Project Skill\n\n**Purpose**: Deploy a new self-hosted service to the Kubernetes cluster from a GitHub repository.\n\n**When to use**: User provides a GitHub URL or project name and wants to deploy it to the cluster.\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Research Phase\n\n**Input**: GitHub repository URL or project name\n\n**Actions**:\n- Visit the GitHub repository\n- Check the README for:\n  - Official Docker image (Docker Hub, ghcr.io, etc.)\n  - docker-compose.yml file\n  - Self-hosting documentation\n  - Required dependencies (PostgreSQL, MySQL, Redis, etc.)\n  - Environment variables needed\n  - Default ports\n  - Storage requirements\n\n**Find Docker Image Priority**:\n1. Check official documentation for recommended image\n2. Look in docker-compose.yml for `image:` directive\n3. Check GitHub Container Registry: `ghcr.io/<org>/<repo>`\n4. Check Docker Hub: `<org>/<repo>`\n5. Check releases page for container images\n6. Last resort: Build from Dockerfile (avoid if possible)\n\n**Extract Configuration**:\n- Container port (default port the app listens on)\n- Environment variables (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_HOST, SMTP, etc.)\n- Volume mounts (what data needs persistence)\n- Dependencies (database type, cache, etc.)\n\n### 2. Database Setup (if needed)\n\n**If project requires PostgreSQL**:\n- User provides database credentials or use pattern: `<service>` user with secure password\n- Database will be created in shared `postgresql.dbaas.svc.cluster.local`\n- Connection string format: `postgresql://<user>:<password>@postgresql.dbaas.svc.cluster.local:5432/<dbname>`\n\n**If project requires MySQL**:\n- User provides database credentials\n- Database in shared `mysql.dbaas.svc.cluster.local`\n- Connection string format: `mysql://<user>:<password>@mysql.dbaas.svc.cluster.local:3306/<dbname>`\n\n**If project requires Redis**:\n- Use shared Redis: `redis.redis.svc.cluster.local:6379`\n- No password required\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Never create databases yourself - always ask user for credentials to use.\n\n### 3. NFS Storage Setup (if service needs persistent data)\n\n**IMPORTANT**: NFS directories must exist and be exported on the NFS server BEFORE deploying the service. If the directory doesn''t exist, the pod will fail to mount the volume and get stuck in `ContainerCreating`.\n\n**Steps**:\n\n1. **Create the directory on the NFS server**:\n```bash\nssh root@10.0.10.15 ''mkdir -p /mnt/main/<service> && chmod 777 /mnt/main/<service>''\n```\n\n2. **Export the directory via TrueNAS**:\n   - The NFS export must be configured in TrueNAS so Kubernetes nodes can mount it\n   - Create the export via TrueNAS WebUI or API, allowing access from the Kubernetes network (10.0.20.0/24)\n   - Verify the export is accessible:\n```bash\n# From a k8s node or the dev VM\nshowmount -e 10.0.10.15 | grep <service>\n```\n\n3. **Verify the mount works before proceeding**:\n```bash\n# Quick test from a k8s node\nssh root@10.0.20.100 ''mount -t nfs 10.0.10.15:/mnt/main/<service> /tmp/test-mount && ls /tmp/test-mount && umount /tmp/test-mount''\n```\n\n**Only proceed to Terraform module creation after confirming the NFS export is accessible.**\n\n### 4. Terraform Module Creation\n\n**Create module directory**:\n```bash\nmkdir -p modules/kubernetes/<service-name>/\n```\n\n**Create `modules/kubernetes/<service-name>/main.tf`**:\n\n```hcl\nvariable \"tls_secret_name\" {}\nvariable \"tier\" { type = string }\nvariable \"postgresql_password\" {}  # Only if needed\n# Add other variables as needed (smtp_password, api_keys, etc.)\n\nresource \"kubernetes_namespace\" \"<service>\" {\n  metadata {\n    name = \"<service>\"\n  }\n}\n\nmodule \"tls_secret\" {\n  source          = \"../setup_tls_secret\"\n  namespace       = kubernetes_namespace.<service>.metadata[0].name\n  tls_secret_name = var.tls_secret_name\n}\n\n# If database migrations needed, add init_container\nresource \"kubernetes_deployment\" \"<service>\" {\n  metadata {\n    name      = \"<service>\"\n    namespace = kubernetes_namespace.<service>.metadata[0].name\n    labels = {\n      app  = \"<service>\"\n      tier = var.tier\n    }\n  }\n  spec {\n    replicas = 1\n    selector {\n      match_labels = {\n        app = \"<service>\"\n      }\n    }\n    template {\n      metadata {\n        labels = {\n          app = \"<service>\"\n        }\n      }\n      spec {\n        # Init container for migrations (if needed)\n        # init_container { ... }\n\n        container {\n          name  = \"<service>\"\n          image = \"<docker-image>:<tag>\"\n\n          port {\n            container_port = <port>\n          }\n\n          # Environment variables\n          env {\n            name  = \"DATABASE_URL\"\n            value = \"postgresql://<service>:${var.postgresql_password}@postgresql.dbaas.svc.cluster.local:5432/<service>\"\n          }\n          # Add other env vars as needed\n\n          # Volume mounts for persistent data\n          volume_mount {\n            name       = \"data\"\n            mount_path = \"<mount-path>\"\n            sub_path   = \"<optional-subpath>\"\n          }\n\n          resources {\n            requests = {\n              memory = \"256Mi\"\n              cpu    = \"100m\"\n            }\n            limits = {\n              memory = \"2Gi\"\n              cpu    = \"1\"\n            }\n          }\n\n          # Health checks (if endpoints exist)\n          liveness_probe {\n            http_get {\n              path = \"/health\"  # or /healthz, /, etc.\n              port = <port>\n            }\n            initial_delay_seconds = 60\n            period_seconds        = 30\n          }\n        }\n\n        # NFS volume for persistence\n        volume {\n          name = \"data\"\n          nfs {\n            server = \"10.0.10.15\"\n            path   = \"/mnt/main/<service>\"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nresource \"kubernetes_service\" \"<service>\" {\n  metadata {\n    name      = \"<service>\"\n    namespace = kubernetes_namespace.<service>.metadata[0].name\n    labels = {\n      app = \"<service>\"\n    }\n  }\n\n  spec {\n    selector = {\n      app = \"<service>\"\n    }\n    port {\n      name        = \"http\"\n      port        = 80\n      target_port = <container-port>\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nmodule \"ingress\" {\n  source          = \"../ingress_factory\"\n  namespace       = kubernetes_namespace.<service>.metadata[0].name\n  name            = \"<service>\"\n  tls_secret_name = var.tls_secret_name\n  # Add extra_annotations if needed (proxy-body-size, timeouts, etc.)\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Update Main Terraform Files\n\n**Add to `modules/kubernetes/main.tf`**:\n\n1. Add variable declarations at top:\n```hcl\nvariable \"<service>_postgresql_password\" { type = string }\n```\n\n2. Add to appropriate DEFCON level (ask user which level, default to 5):\n```hcl\n5 : [\n  ...,\n  \"<service>\"\n]\n```\n\n3. Add module block at bottom:\n```hcl\nmodule \"<service>\" {\n  source              = \"./<service>\"\n  for_each            = contains(local.active_modules, \"<service>\") ? { <service> = true } : {}\n  tls_secret_name     = var.tls_secret_name\n  postgresql_password = var.<service>_postgresql_password\n  tier                = local.tiers.aux  # or appropriate tier\n\n  depends_on = [null_resource.core_services]\n}\n```\n\n**Add to `main.tf`**:\n\n1. Add variable:\n```hcl\nvariable \"<service>_postgresql_password\" { type = string }\n```\n\n2. Pass to kubernetes_cluster module:\n```hcl\nmodule \"kubernetes_cluster\" {\n  ...\n  <service>_postgresql_password = var.<service>_postgresql_password\n}\n```\n\n**Update `terraform.tfvars`**:\n\n1. Add password/credentials:\n```hcl\n<service>_postgresql_password = \"<secure-password>\"\n```\n\n2. Add to Cloudflare DNS (ask user if proxied or non-proxied):\n```hcl\ncloudflare_non_proxied_names = [\n  ...,\n  \"<service>\"\n]\n```\n\n### 6. Email/SMTP Configuration (if needed)\n\nIf service needs to send emails:\n```hcl\nenv {\n  name  = \"MAILER_HOST\"\n  value = \"mailserver.viktorbarzin.me\"  # Public hostname for TLS\n}\nenv {\n  name  = \"MAILER_PORT\"\n  value = \"587\"\n}\nenv {\n  name  = \"MAILER_USER\"\n  value = \"info@viktorbarzin.me\"\n}\nenv {\n  name  = \"MAILER_PASSWORD\"\n  value = var.mailserver_accounts[\"info@viktorbarzin.me\"]  # Pass from module\n}\n```\n\nAdd to module call:\n```hcl\nsmtp_password = var.mailserver_accounts[\"info@viktorbarzin.me\"]\n```\n\n### 7. Apply Terraform\n\n```bash\nterraform init\nterraform apply -target=module.kubernetes_cluster.module.<service> -var=\"kube_config_path=$(pwd)/config\" -auto-approve\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT: Also apply the cloudflared module to create the Cloudflare DNS record:**\n```bash\nterraform apply -target=module.kubernetes_cluster.module.cloudflared -var=\"kube_config_path=$(pwd)/config\" -auto-approve\n```\nWithout this step, the DNS record won''t be created even though it''s defined in `terraform.tfvars`.\n\n### 8. Verification\n\n```bash\nkubectl get pods -n <service>\nkubectl logs -n <service> -l app=<service> --tail=50\n```\n\nTest URL: `https://<service>.viktorbarzin.me`\n\n### 9. Commit Changes\n\n```bash\ngit add modules/kubernetes/<service>/ main.tf modules/kubernetes/main.tf terraform.tfvars\ngit commit -m \"Add <service> deployment\n\n- Deploy <service> as <description>\n- Uses <dependencies>\n- Ingress at <service>.viktorbarzin.me\n\n[ci skip]\"\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Init Container for Migrations\n```hcl\ninit_container {\n  name    = \"migration\"\n  image   = \"<same-image>\"\n  command = [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"<migration-command>\"]\n\n  # Same env vars and volumes as main container\n}\n```\n\n### Dynamic Environment Variables\n```hcl\nlocals {\n  common_env = [\n    { name = \"VAR1\", value = \"value1\" },\n    { name = \"VAR2\", value = \"value2\" },\n  ]\n}\n\ndynamic \"env\" {\n  for_each = local.common_env\n  content {\n    name  = env.value.name\n    value = env.value.value\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### External URL Configuration\nMany apps need their public URL configured:\n```hcl\nenv {\n  name  = \"APP_URL\"  # or PUBLIC_URL, EXTERNAL_URL, etc.\n  value = \"https://<service>.viktorbarzin.me\"\n}\nenv {\n  name  = \"HTTPS\"  # or ENABLE_HTTPS, etc.\n  value = \"true\"\n}\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Find official Docker image or docker-compose\n- [ ] Identify dependencies (DB, Redis, etc.)\n- [ ] Ask user for database credentials (never create yourself)\n- [ ] Create NFS directory and export on TrueNAS (if persistent storage needed)\n- [ ] Verify NFS mount is accessible from k8s nodes\n- [ ] Create `modules/kubernetes/<service>/main.tf`\n- [ ] Update `modules/kubernetes/main.tf` (variables, DEFCON level, module block)\n- [ ] Update `main.tf` (variable, pass to module)\n- [ ] Update `terraform.tfvars` (password, Cloudflare DNS)\n- [ ] Run `terraform init` and `terraform apply`\n- [ ] Verify pods are running\n- [ ] Test the URL\n- [ ] Commit changes with `[ci skip]`\n\n## Questions to Ask User\n\n1. What DEFCON level should this service be in? (Default: 5)\n2. Should Cloudflare proxy this domain? (Default: no, add to non_proxied_names)\n3. Does this need email/SMTP? (Configure if yes)\n4. What database credentials should I use? (Never create yourself)\n5. What tier? (core/cluster/gpu/edge/aux - default: aux)\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Always create NFS directories and exports BEFORE deploying** - pods will get stuck in `ContainerCreating` if the NFS path doesn''t exist or isn''t exported\n- **Always use official documentation** as the source of truth\n- **Prefer stable/latest tags** over specific versions for self-hosted\n- **Use shared infrastructure**: PostgreSQL at `postgresql.dbaas.svc.cluster.local`, Redis at `redis.redis.svc.cluster.local`\n- **NFS storage**: Always at `10.0.10.15:/mnt/main/<service>`\n- **Email**: Use `mailserver.viktorbarzin.me` (public hostname) not internal service name\n- **Resource limits**: Start conservative, can increase if needed\n- **Health checks**: Only add if the app has health endpoints\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-27T01:56:16.070Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Kubernetes-focused AI Agents needing automated deployment of self-hosted services from GitHub repositories.","zh":"非常适合专注于 Kubernetes 的 AI Agent，需要从 GitHub 仓库自动部署自托管服务。","ja":"Kubernetes に焦点を当てた AI Agent にとって理想的であり、GitHub リポジトリからセルフホスト型サービスを自動デプロイする必要がある場合に最適です。","ko":"Kubernetes에 중점을 둔 AI 에이전트에게 이상적이며, GitHub 저장소에서 셀프 호스팅 서비스의 자동화된 배포가 필요한 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial centrados en Kubernetes que necesitan una implementación automatizada de servicios autohospedados desde repositorios de GitHub.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur Kubernetes nécessitant un déploiement automatisé de services auto-hébergés à partir de référentiels GitHub.","de":"Ideal für kubernetes-fokussierte KI-Agents, die eine automatisierte Bereitstellung von selbstgehosteten Diensten aus GitHub-Repositorys benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA focados em Kubernetes que necessitam de implantação automatizada de serviços auto-hospedados de repositórios do GitHub.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Kubernetes, которым необходима автоматизированная развертка selbst-хостинговых сервисов из репозиториев GitHub.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الإي الأي التي تركز على Kubernetes وتحتاج إلى تثبيت تلقائي لخدمات الاستضافة الذاتية من مستودعات GitHub."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to deploy new services to Kubernetes clusters using GitHub repository URLs or project names, leveraging docker-compose.yml files and official Docker images from Docker Hub or ghcr.io.","zh":"使 Agent 能够使用 GitHub 仓库 URL 或项目名称，利用 docker-compose.yml 文件和来自 Docker Hub 或 ghcr.io 的官方 Docker 镜像，将新服务部署到 Kubernetes 集群。","ja":"GitHub リポジトリの URL またはプロジェクト名を使用して、docker-compose.yml ファイルと Docker Hub または ghcr.io からの公式 Docker イメージを活用し、Kubernetes クラスターに新しいサービスをデプロイする機能を Agent に付与します。","ko":"GitHub 저장소 URL 또는 프로젝트 이름을 사용하여, docker-compose.yml 파일과 Docker Hub 또는 ghcr.io의 공식 Docker 이미지를 활용해 Kubernetes 클러스터에 새로운 서비스를 배포할 수 있는 능력을 에이전트에게 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar nuevos servicios en clusters de Kubernetes utilizando direcciones URL de repositorios de GitHub o nombres de proyectos, aprovechando archivos docker-compose.yml y imágenes oficiales de Docker de Docker Hub o ghcr.io.","fr":"Permet aux agents de déployer de nouveaux services sur des clusters Kubernetes à l''aide d''URL de référentiels GitHub ou de noms de projets, en exploitant les fichiers docker-compose.yml et les images officielles Docker de Docker Hub ou ghcr.io.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, neue Dienste in Kubernetes-Clustern bereitzustellen, indem sie GitHub-Repository-URLs oder Projektname verwenden, wobei docker-compose.yml-Dateien und offizielle Docker-Images von Docker Hub oder ghcr.io genutzt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implantar novos serviços em clusters Kubernetes usando URLs de repositórios do GitHub ou nomes de projetos, aproveitando arquivos docker-compose.yml e imagens oficiais do Docker do Docker Hub ou ghcr.io.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью развертки новых сервисов в кластерах Kubernetes, используя URL-адреса репозиториев GitHub или имена проектов, опираясь на файлы docker-compose.yml и официальные образы Docker из Docker Hub или ghcr.io.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من نشر خدمات جديدة إلى مجموعات Kubernetes باستخدام عناوين URL لمستودعات GitHub أو أسماء مشاريع، مستفيداً من ملفات docker-compose.yml والصور الرسمية للدッカー من Docker Hub أو ghcr.io."},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying self-hosted services to Kubernetes clusters","Automating service deployment from GitHub repositories","Validating self-hosting documentation for compatibility"],"zh":["将自托管服务部署到 Kubernetes 集群","从 GitHub 仓库自动化服务部署","验证自托管文档的兼容性"],"ja":["セルフホスト型サービスを Kubernetes クラスターにデプロイ","GitHub リポジトリからのサービスデプロイの自動化","互換性のためのセルフホスティングドキュメントの検証"],"ko":["Kubernetes 클러스터에 셀프 호스팅 서비스 배포","GitHub 저장소에서 서비스 배포 자동화","호환성을 위한 셀프 호스팅 문서 검증"],"es":["Implementación de servicios autohospedados en clusters de Kubernetes","Automatización de la implementación de servicios desde repositorios de GitHub","Validación de la documentación de autohospedaje para la compatibilidad"],"fr":["Déploiement de services auto-hébergés sur des clusters Kubernetes","Automatisation du déploiement de services à partir de référentiels GitHub","Validation de la documentation d''auto-hébergement pour la compatibilité"],"de":["Bereitstellung von selbstgehosteten Diensten in Kubernetes-Clustern","Automatisierung der Bereitstellung von Diensten aus GitHub-Repositorys","Überprüfung der Dokumentation zur Selbsthosting für die Kompatibilität"],"pt":["Implantação de serviços auto-hospedados em clusters Kubernetes","Automatização da implantação de serviços de repositórios do GitHub","Validação da documentação de auto-hospedagem para compatibilidade"],"ru":["Развертка selbst-хостинговых сервисов в кластерах Kubernetes","Автоматизация развертки сервисов из репозиториев GitHub","Проверка документации по self-хостингу на совместимость"],"ar":["نشر خدمات الاستضافة الذاتية إلى مجموعات Kubernetes","تأتمة نشر الخدمات من مستودعات GitHub","التحقق من توثيق الاستضافة الذاتية لتحقق التوافق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to a Kubernetes cluster","Needs a valid GitHub repository URL or project name","Dependent on the presence of docker-compose.yml and official Docker images"],"zh":["需要访问 Kubernetes 集群","需要有效的 GitHub 仓库 URL 或项目名称","依赖于 docker-compose.yml 和官方 Docker 镜像的存在"],"ja":["Kubernetes クラスターへのアクセスが必要","有効な GitHub リポジトリ URL またはプロジェクト名が必要","docker-compose.yml と公式 Docker イメージの存在に依存"],"ko":["Kubernetes 클러스터에 대한 액세스 필요","유효한 GitHub 저장소 URL 또는 프로젝트 이름 필요","docker-compose.yml 및 공식 Docker 이미지의 존재에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a un cluster de Kubernetes","Necesita una dirección URL de repositorio de GitHub válida o un nombre de proyecto","Depende de la presencia de archivos docker-compose.yml y de imágenes oficiales de Docker"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à un cluster Kubernetes","Nécessite une URL de référentiel GitHub valide ou un nom de projet","Dépend de la présence de fichiers docker-compose.yml et d''images officielles Docker"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf einen Kubernetes-Cluster","Benötigt eine gültige GitHub-Repository-URL oder einen Projektname","Hängt von der Anwesenheit von docker-compose.yml-Dateien und offiziellen Docker-Images ab"],"pt":["Exige acesso a um cluster Kubernetes","Necessita de uma URL de repositório do GitHub válida ou nome de projeto","Depende da presença de arquivos docker-compose.yml e imagens oficiais do Docker"],"ru":["Требует доступа к кластеру Kubernetes","Требует действительного URL-адреса репозитория GitHub или имени проекта","Зависит от наличия файлов docker-compose.yml и официальных образов Docker"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مجموعة Kubernetes","يحتاج إلى عنوان URL صالح لمستودع GitHub أو اسم مشروع","يعتمد على وجود ملفات docker-compose.yml والصور الرسمية للدッカー"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"f5eb776d58567646f34dda6c4961fa0cdccd2d84d3b55e9ac8b48639f3a69da8","qualityScore":42}');
