ra criar aplicações","Suporte a MCP skills","Integração com React e Node.js"],"ru":["Чистая и простая архитектура","Шаблон маршрутизатора приложений Next.js","Инструмент ИИ для создания приложений","Поддержка MCP skills","Интеграция с React и Node.js"],"ar":["هندسة نظيفة و بسيطة","قالب روتير التطبيقات Next.js","أداة ذكاء اصطناعي لإنشاء التطبيقات","دعم مهارات MCP","التكامل مع React و Node.js"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Next.js应用路由","clean架构","MCP技能","仓库模板","快速构建","开发效率","如何使用Next.js","什么是clean架构"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Next.jsアプリルーター","cleanアーキテクチャ","MCPスキル","リポジトリテンプレート","迅速な構築","開発効率","Next.jsの使い方","cleanアーキテクチャとは"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Next.js 애플리케이션 라우터","클린 아키텍처","MCP 기술","저장소 템플릿","빠른 구축","개발 효율성","Next.js 사용 방법","클린 아키텍처란"],"es":["herramientas de ai","next.js","router","arquitectura limpia","desarrollo web","cómo usar next.js","alternativas a next.js","instalación de next.js","guía de configuración de next.js"],"fr":["outils d''ia","next.js","routeur","architecture propre","développement web","comment utiliser next.js","alternatives à next.js","installation de next.js","guide de configuration de next.js"],"de":["ki-tools","next.js","router","saubere architektur","webentwicklung","wie man next.js verwendet","alternativen zu next.js","installation von next.js","konfigurationsanleitung für next.js"],"pt":["como usar Next.js","o que é modelo de roteador de aplicativos","ferramentas de IA para desenvolvedores","Next.js vs React","guia de instalação do Next.js","modelo de roteador de aplicativos Next.js","desenvolvimento de aplicações com Next.js","arquitetura de aplicações Next.js"],"ru":["как использовать Next.js","что такое шаблон маршрутизатора приложений","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","Next.js vs React","руководство по установке Next.js","шаблон маршрутизатора приложений Next.js","разработка приложений с Next.js","архитектура приложений Next.js"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام Next.js","ما هو قالب روتير التطبيقات","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","Next.js vs React","دليل تثبيت Next.js","قالب روتير التطبيقات Next.js","تطوير التطبيقات مع Next.js","هندسة التطبيقات Next.js"]}},"owner":"jorggerojas","repo":"next-skeleton-app","repoPath":"jorggerojas/next-skeleton-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.825Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hierarchy","description":"Define the components hierarchy, how to use components inside pages and how to mix components and when its needed to create new ones.","bodyPreview":"# Component Hierarchy\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Server Components fetch data** - Server Components fetch data directly, Client Components receive data as props\n2. **Atomic Design** - Build from atoms → molecules → organisms → pages\n3. **Hooks in Client Components** - Custom hooks belong in Client Components (organisms), not Server Components\n4. **Performance & SEO first** - Always prioritize unless there''s an edge case\n5. **Never use `any`** - Under no circumstances\n\n## Atomic Design Hierarchy","body":"# Component Hierarchy\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Server Components fetch data** - Server Components fetch data directly, Client Components receive data as props\n2. **Atomic Design** - Build from atoms → molecules → organisms → pages\n3. **Hooks in Client Components** - Custom hooks belong in Client Components (organisms), not Server Components\n4. **Performance & SEO first** - Always prioritize unless there''s an edge case\n5. **Never use `any`** - Under no circumstances\n\n## Atomic Design Hierarchy\n\n```txt\nPage (src/app/)\n└── Organism (large component with business logic)\n    └── Molecule (group of atoms with simple logic)\n        └── Atom (single UI element, no logic)\n```\n\n### Atoms\n\nSingle UI elements with no business logic. Receive props, render UI.\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/Button/Button.tsx\ninterface ButtonProps {\n  children: ReactNode;\n  onClick?: () => void;\n  variant?: \"primary\" | \"secondary\";\n  disabled?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport default function Button({ children, onClick, variant = \"primary\", disabled }: ButtonProps) {\n  return (\n    <button onClick={onClick} disabled={disabled} className={`btn btn-${variant}`}>\n      {children}\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/Input/Input.tsx\ninterface InputProps {\n  value: string;\n  onChange: (value: string) => void;\n  placeholder?: string;\n  type?: \"text\" | \"email\" | \"password\";\n}\n\nexport default function Input({ value, onChange, placeholder, type = \"text\" }: InputProps) {\n  const handleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    onChange(e.target.value);\n  };\n\n  return <input type={type} value={value} onChange={handleChange} placeholder={placeholder} />;\n}\n```\n\n### Molecules\n\nGroup of atoms with simple interaction logic. No hooks, no data fetching.\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/SearchInput/SearchInput.tsx\nimport Input from \"../Input\";\nimport Button from \"../Button\";\n\ninterface SearchInputProps {\n  value: string;\n  onChange: (value: string) => void;\n  onSearch: () => void;\n  placeholder?: string;\n}\n\nexport default function SearchInput({ value, onChange, onSearch, placeholder }: SearchInputProps) {\n  const handleKeyDown = (e: React.KeyboardEvent) => {\n    if (e.key === \"Enter\") {\n      onSearch();\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex gap-2\" onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}>\n      <Input value={value} onChange={onChange} placeholder={placeholder} />\n      <Button onClick={onSearch}>Search</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/UserCard/UserCard.tsx\nimport Avatar from \"../Avatar\";\nimport Badge from \"../Badge\";\n\ninterface UserCardProps {\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n  avatarUrl?: string;\n  role: \"admin\" | \"user\";\n}\n\nexport default function UserCard({ name, email, avatarUrl, role }: UserCardProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex items-center gap-4 p-4 border rounded\">\n      <Avatar src={avatarUrl} alt={name} />\n      <div>\n        <h3 className=\"font-bold\">{name}</h3>\n        <p className=\"text-gray-500\">{email}</p>\n      </div>\n      <Badge variant={role === \"admin\" ? \"primary\" : \"secondary\"}>{role}</Badge>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Organisms\n\nLarge components with business logic. Can use hooks, stores, and handle complex interactions.\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/UserList/UserList.tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useDebounce } from \"@/hooks\";\nimport { useUIStore } from \"@/stores\";\nimport SearchInput from \"../SearchInput\";\nimport UserCard from \"../UserCard\";\n\ninterface User {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n  avatarUrl?: string;\n  role: \"admin\" | \"user\";\n}\n\ninterface UserListProps {\n  users: User[];\n  onUserSelect: (user: User) => void;\n}\n\nexport default function UserList({ users, onUserSelect }: UserListProps) {\n  const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState(\"\");\n  const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(searchTerm, 300);\n  const { openModal } = useUIStore();\n\n  const filteredUsers = users.filter(\n    (user) =>\n      user.name.toLowerCase().includes(debouncedSearch.toLowerCase()) ||\n      user.email.toLowerCase().includes(debouncedSearch.toLowerCase())\n  );\n\n  const handleUserClick = (user: User) => {\n    onUserSelect(user);\n    openModal();\n  };\n\n  const handleSearch = () => {\n    // Optional: trigger immediate search\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"space-y-4\">\n      <SearchInput\n        value={searchTerm}\n        onChange={setSearchTerm}\n        onSearch={handleSearch}\n        placeholder=\"Search users...\"\n      />\n      <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n        {filteredUsers.map((user) => (\n          <div key={user.id} onClick={() => handleUserClick(user)} className=\"cursor-pointer\">\n            <UserCard {...user} />\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pages (Server Components)\n\nServer Components fetch data directly. Client Components receive data as props.\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\nimport { UserList } from \"@/components\";\n\nasync function getUsers() {\n  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\", {\n    next: { revalidate: 60 },\n  });\n  return res.json();\n}\n\nexport default async function UsersPage() {\n  const users = await getUsers();\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Users</h1>\n      <UserList users={users} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pages (Client Components)\n\nWhen you need interactivity, use Client Components:\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { UserList } from \"@/components\";\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport default function UsersPage() {\n  const { data: users, isLoading } = useUsers();\n\n  const handleUserSelect = (user: { id: string; name: string }) => {\n    console.log(\"Selected user:\", user.id);\n  };\n\n  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>;\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Users</h1>\n      <UserList users={users} onUserSelect={handleUserSelect} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Data Flow\n\n```txt\nServer Data Flow (Server Components):\nAPI → Server Component (fetch) → Organism → Molecule → Atom\n                                 (props)    (props)   (props)\n\nClient Data Flow (Client Components):\nAPI → React Query Hook → Client Component → Organism → Molecule → Atom\n                         (props)           (props)    (props)   (props)\n\nClient State Flow:\nUser Action → Atom (onClick) → Molecule (handler) → Organism (hook/store) → UI Update\n```\n\n## When to Create a New Component\n\n| Scenario | Create New? | Level |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| Button with icon | No, add `icon` prop to Button | Atom |\n| Search bar (input + button) | Yes | Molecule |\n| Form with validation | Yes | Organism |\n| Repeating UI pattern (3+ times) | Yes | Appropriate level |\n| Single-use complex UI | Maybe, if >100 lines | Organism |\n\n## Hook Usage Rules\n\n| Component Level | Can Use Hooks? | Examples |\n|-----------------|----------------|----------|\n| Atom | No | Button, Input, Badge |\n| Molecule | Rarely (only `useState` for local UI) | SearchInput, FormField |\n| Organism | Yes | UserList, DataTable, Forms |\n| Page | Only for client-side mutations | useUsers.create() |\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ BAD: Hook in atom\nexport default function Button({ label }) {\n  const { isLoading } = useUIStore(); // DON''T\n  return <button>{label}</button>;\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Props in atom\nexport default function Button({ label, isLoading }) {\n  return <button disabled={isLoading}>{label}</button>;\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Hook in organism\nexport default function UserForm({ onSubmit }) {\n  const { isLoading, setLoading } = useUIStore();\n  const [formData, setFormData] = useState({});\n\n  const handleSubmit = async () => {\n    setLoading(true);\n    await onSubmit(formData);\n    setLoading(false);\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>\n      <Input value={formData.name} onChange={(v) => setFormData({ ...formData, name: v })} />\n      <Button isLoading={isLoading}>Submit</Button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Server vs Client Data\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ GOOD: Server Component fetches data directly\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\nasync function getUsers() {\n  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\");\n  return res.json();\n}\n\nexport default async function UsersPage() {\n  const users = await getUsers();\n  return <UserList users={users} />;\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Client Component with hooks for interactivity\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport default function UsersPage() {\n  const { data: users } = useUsers();\n  return <UserList users={users} />;\n}\n\n// Component receives data as props\nexport default function UserList({ users }: { users: User[] }) {\n  return <div>{users.map(...)}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n## Client-Side Mutations\n\nFor mutations (create, update, delete), use hooks in Client Components:\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport default function UsersPage() {\n  const { data: users } = useUsers();\n  const createUser = useUsers.create();\n  const deleteUser = useUsers.delete();\n\n  const handleCreate = (data: CreateUserInput) => {\n    createUser.mutate(data);\n  };\n\n  const handleDelete = (id: string) => {\n    deleteUser.mutate(id);\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <UserForm onSubmit={handleCreate} />\n      <UserList users={users} onDelete={handleDelete} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **Server Components fetch data directly** - No hooks needed\n- **Client Components use hooks** - For interactivity and mutations\n- **Props down, events up** - Data flows down, actions bubble up via callbacks\n- **Keep atoms pure** - No side effects, no hooks, just UI\n- **Organisms are the brain** - Business logic lives here\n- **Test at the right level** - Unit test atoms, integration test organisms\n- **Never use `any`** - Define proper types for all props and state\n- **Handler naming** - `handle*` inside components, `on*` for props from parents\n- **Prefer composition** - Build complex UIs by combining simple components\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:41:08.741Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Next.js App Development Agents requiring a structured architecture with Server and Client Components","zh":"适用于需要结构化架构的 Server 和 Client 组件的 Next.js 应用开发代理","ja":"構造化されたアーキテクチャを持つServerとClientコンポーネントを必要とするNext.jsアプリ開発エージェントに適しています","ko":"구조화된 아키텍처를 갖는 Server와 Client 컴포넌트가 필요한 Next.js 애플리케이션 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo de Aplicaciones Next.js que requieren una arquitectura estructurada con Componentes de Servidor y Cliente","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents de Développement d''Applications Next.js nécessitant une architecture structurée avec des Composants Serveur et Client","de":"Ideal für Next.js-App-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine strukturierte Architektur mit Server- und Client-Komponenten erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Aplicativos Next.js que exigem uma arquitetura estruturada com Componentes de Servidor e Cliente","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки приложений Next.js, требующих структурированной архитектуры с компонентами сервера и клиента","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزج التطبيقي Next.js الذين يتطلبون هيكلاً معماريًا منظمًا مع مكونات الخادم والعميل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build scalable applications using Atomic Design principles, prioritizing performance and SEO, and leveraging custom hooks in Client Components with strict type checking, avoiding the use of ''any''","zh":"赋予代理构建可扩展应用的能力，使用原子设计原则，优先考虑性能和SEO，并在客户端组件中使用自定义钩子，具有严格的类型检查，避免使用 ''any''","ja":"Atomic Designの原則を使用して拡張可能なアプリケーションを構築する能力をエージェントに与え、パフォーマンスとSEOを優先し、クライアントコンポーネントでカスタムフックを使用し、厳格な型チェックを行い、''any''の使用を避ける","ko":"에이전트가 원자적 설계 원칙을 사용하여 확장 가능한 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 성능과 SEO를 우선시하고, 클라이언트 컴포넌트에서 사용자 정의 훅을 사용하고, 엄格한 형식 검사를 하며 ''any''의 사용을 피합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir aplicaciones escalables utilizando principios de Diseño Atómico, priorizando el rendimiento y el SEO, y aprovechando ganchos personalizados en Componentes de Cliente con una verificación de tipo estricta, evitando el uso de ''any''","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des applications évolutives en utilisant les principes de Conception Atomique, en donnant la priorité aux performances et au SEO, et en exploitant des crochets personnalisés dans les Composants Client avec une vérification de type stricte, en évitant l''utilisation de ''any''","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, skalierbare Anwendungen mit Atomic-Design-Prinzipien zu erstellen, die Leistung und SEO priorisieren und benutzerdefinierte Hooks in Client-Komponenten mit strenger Typüberprüfung nutzen, wobei der Einsatz von ''any'' vermieden wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicações escaláveis usando princípios de Design Atômico, priorizando o desempenho e o SEO, e aproveitando ganchos personalizados em Componentes de Cliente com verificação de tipo estrita, evitando o uso de ''any''","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать масштабируемые приложения, используя принципы атомарного дизайна, отдающие приоритет производительности и SEO, и использующие пользовательские крючки в компонентах клиента со строгой проверкой типов, избегая использования ''any''","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على بناء تطبيقات قابلة للتوسعة باستخدام مبادئ التصميم الذري، وأعطاء الأولوية للأداء و تحسين محركات البحث، والاستفادة من المشابك المخصصة في مكونات العميل مع التحقق الصارم من النوع، وتجنب استخدام ''any''"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular page structures with atoms, molecules, and organisms","Implementing Server Components to fetch data directly for improved performance","Optimizing application architecture for better SEO and user experience"],"zh":["使用原子、分子和生物体设计模块化页面结构","实现Server组件以直接获取数据并提高性能","优化应用程序架构以获得更好的SEO和用户体验"],"ja":["アトム、モレキュール、生物体を使用してモジュラーなページ構造を設計する","サーバーコンポーネントを実装してデータを直接取得し、パフォーマンスを向上させる","アプリケーションのアーキテクチャを最適化してSEOとユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させる"],"ko":["원자, 분자, 생물체를 사용하여 모듈화된 페이지 구조를 설계함","서버 컴포넌트를 구현하여 데이터를 직접 가져와 성능을 개선함","애플리케이션 아키텍처를 최적화하여 SEO와 사용자 경험을 향상시키는 것"],"es":["Diseñar estructuras de página modulares con átomos, moléculas y organismos","Implementar Componentes de Servidor para recuperar datos directamente para mejorar el rendimiento","Optimizar la arquitectura de la aplicación para un mejor SEO y experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Concevoir des structures de page modulaires avec des atomes, des molécules et des organismes","Mettre en œuvre des Composants Serveur pour récupérer des données directement pour améliorer les performances","Optimiser l''architecture de l''application pour un meilleur SEO et une meilleure expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Modulare Seitenstrukturen mit Atomen, Molekülen und Organismen entwerfen","Server-Komponenten implementieren, um Daten direkt abzurufen und die Leistung zu verbessern","Anwendungsarchitektur optimieren, um ein besseres SEO und eine bessere Benutzererfahrung zu erzielen"],"pt":["Projetar estruturas de página modulares com átomos, moléculas e organismos","Implementar Componentes de Servidor para buscar dados diretamente para melhorar o desempenho","Otimizar a arquitetura da aplicação para melhor SEO e experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Проектировать модульные структуры страниц с атомами, молекулами и организмами","Реализовывать компоненты сервера для прямого извлечения данных для улучшения производительности","Оптимизировать архитектуру приложения для лучшего SEO и пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["تصميم هياكل صفحة متعددة مع ذرات وجزيئات وأحياء","تنفيذ مكونات الخادم لاسترجاع البيانات مباشرة لتحسين الأداء","تحسين هيكل التطبيق لتحسين محركات البحث وتجربة المستخدم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to strict architecture principles","Must avoid using ''any'' for type checking","Limited to Next.js applications"],"zh":["需要遵守严格的架构原则","必须避免使用 ''any'' 进行类型检查","仅限于Next.js应用"],"ja":["厳格なアーキテクチャ原則に従う必要がある","型チェックに''any''を使用しないこと","Next.jsアプリケーションに限定される"],"ko":["엄격한 아키텍처 원칙을 따라야 함","형식 검사에 ''any''를 사용하지 않아야 함","Next.js 애플리케이션에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a principios de arquitectura estrictos","Debe evitar el uso de ''any'' para la verificación de tipo","Limitado a aplicaciones Next.js"],"fr":["Nécessite d''adhérer à des principes d''architecture stricts","Doit éviter l''utilisation de ''any'' pour la vérification de type","Limité aux applications Next.js"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung strenger Architekturprinzipien","Sollte den Einsatz von ''any'' für die Typüberprüfung vermeiden","Begrenzt auf Next.js-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Exige aderência a princípios de arquitetura estritos","Deve evitar o uso de ''any'' para verificação de tipo","Limitado a aplicações Next.js"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения строгих принципов архитектуры","Должен избегать использования ''any'' для проверки типа","Ограничен приложениями Next.js"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بمبادئ معمارية صارمة","يجب تجنب استخدام ''any'' للتحقق من النوع","محدود بتطبيقات Next.js"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"bc785b079f6495a95f2a7b9570f42ece5c17d9b66e68f361596fd30a6032c5cf","qualityScore":42}');
