s de Windows","Integración con herramientas de AI","Mejora de la seguridad y la compatibilidad","Optimización del rendimiento de las aplicaciones","Implementación de estándares de industria"],"fr":["Connaissances sur les protocoles Windows","Intégration avec des outils d''IA","Amélioration de la sécurité et de la compatibilité","Optimisation des performances des applications","Mise en œuvre de normes industrielles"],"de":["Kenntnisse über Windows-Protokolle","Integration mit KI-Tools","Verbesserung der Sicherheit und Kompatibilität","Optimierung der Leistung von Anwendungen","Umsetzung von Branchenstandards"],"pt":["Especificação aberta do Windows","Protocolos para desenvolvedores","Ferramentas de AI para melhorar a produtividade","Integração com React, Python e Node.js","Suporte à CLI"],"ru":["Открытые спецификации Windows","Протоколы для разработчиков","ИИ Агенты для повышения производительности","Интеграция с React, Python и Node.js","Поддержка CLI"],"ar":["مواصفات ويندوز المفتوحة","بروتوكولات لمن-developers","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي لتحسين الإنتاجية","التكامل مع React, Python و Node.js","دعم CLI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Windows协议","AI智能代理","Microsoft Open Specifications","Windows API","如何使用Windows协议","Windows协议开发教程","Windows协议与API的区别"],"ja":["Windowsプロトコル","AIエージェント","Microsoft Open Specifications","Windows API","Windowsプロトコルの使用方法","Windowsプロトコルの開発ガイド","WindowsプロトコルとAPIの違い"],"ko":["Windows 프로토콜","AI 에이전트","Microsoft Open Specifications","Windows API","Windows 프로토콜 사용 방법","Windows 프로토콜 개발 가이드","Windows 프로토콜과 API의 차이"],"es":["cómo utilizar protocolos de Windows","herramientas de AI para desarrolladores","protocolos de Windows vs SOAP","instalación de protocolos de Windows","guía de configuración de protocolos de Windows","mejora del rendimiento de aplicaciones con protocolos de Windows"],"fr":["comment utiliser les protocoles Windows","outils d''IA pour les développeurs","protocoles Windows vs SOAP","installation des protocoles Windows","guide de configuration des protocoles Windows","amélioration des performances des applications avec les protocoles Windows"],"de":["wie man Windows-Protokolle verwendet","KI-Tools für Entwickler","Windows-Protokolle vs SOAP","Installation von Windows-Protokollen","Konfigurationsanleitung für Windows-Protokolle","Leistungsverbesserung von Anwendungen mit Windows-Protokollen"],"pt":["como usar Ferramentas de AI","o que é Windows Protocols","Ferramentas de AI alternative","Ferramentas de AI vs outros","instalar Ferramentas de AI","guias de configuração de Ferramentas de AI"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое Windows Protocols","ИИ Агенты alternative","ИИ Агенты vs другие","установить ИИ Агенты","руководства по настройке ИИ Агентов"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","ما هي بروتوكولات ويندوز","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي بديلة","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي مقابل أخرى","تثبيت أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","دلائل إعداد أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"awakecoding","repo":"openspecs","repoPath":"awakecoding/openspecs","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.960Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"windows-protocols","description":"Local Microsoft Open Specifications corpus navigator for Windows protocols. Use this skill when the user asks protocol-level questions, needs message/structure details, wants section-by-section summaries, or needs cross-references across related specifications.","bodyPreview":"# Windows Protocols Corpus Navigator\n\n## Overview\n\n- The markdown corpus is already extracted locally, next to `SKILL.md`.\n- Use local files only. Do not use network lookup for this skill.\n- Do not run download or setup commands as part of normal usage.\n\nThis skill is optimized for structure-first navigation of Microsoft Open Specifications markdown and evidence-grounded answers.\n\n## Corpus Layout\n\n- `README.md` — index with three sections: Overview Documents (domain maps), Technical Documents (","body":"# Windows Protocols Corpus Navigator\n\n## Overview\n\n- The markdown corpus is already extracted locally, next to `SKILL.md`.\n- Use local files only. Do not use network lookup for this skill.\n- Do not run download or setup commands as part of normal usage.\n\nThis skill is optimized for structure-first navigation of Microsoft Open Specifications markdown and evidence-grounded answers.\n\n## Corpus Layout\n\n- `README.md` — index with three sections: Overview Documents (domain maps), Technical Documents (full spec list), and Reference Documents. Overview Documents are at the top; use them for topical discovery.\n- `LEGAL.md` — legal and redistribution notice.\n- `<PROTOCOL-ID>/` — protocol directories (Overview, Technical, or Reference), directly under this folder.\n- `<PROTOCOL-ID>/<PROTOCOL-ID>.md` — primary markdown spec content.\n- `<PROTOCOL-ID>/media/` — extracted figures and image assets referenced by the markdown.\n\n## Corpus Document Types\n\n- **Overview Documents** — Domain maps that group related protocols under a topic (file access, authentication, storage, remote desktop, etc.). Each describes system capabilities, lists member protocols with their roles, and contains many links to specifications. Use as the primary entry point for topical discovery.\n- **Technical Documents** — Individual protocol specifications with full wire-format, message syntax, and behavior details.\n- **Reference Documents** — Supplemental references (error codes, shared types, etc.).\n\n## Protocol Clusters by Domain\n\nWhen using Overview documents for discovery, expect these cluster themes:\n\n- **Authentication**: Kerberos, NTLM, SPNEGO — core for file access, RDP, Group Policy.\n- **File Access**: SMB/CIFS family, DFS, WebDAV, shared types (FSCC, FSA).\n- **Remote Desktop**: Base + graphics pipeline, gateway, virtual channels (clipboard, devices, transport).\n- **Storage**: Disk/volume management, shadow copies, EFS, backup, removable media.\n- **Group Policy**: Core protocol + extensions; depends on AD and file access.\n- **Network Access Protection**: SoH/SoHR over PEAP; DHCP/VPN/TSGU/IPsec enforcement.\n- **Content Caching**: Peer discovery, retrieval, hosted cache; integrates with SMB/HTTP.\n- **File Services Management**: FSRM, remote VSS, classification.\n- **Rights Management**: Publish/consume protected content.\n- **Virtual Storage**: Remote shared virtual disks over SMB.\n\n## Protocol Naming and Scope\n\n- `MS-...` documents are Microsoft protocol specifications (wire formats, behavior, state machines, structures).\n- Families share prefixes (for example `MS-RDP*`, `MS-AD*`, `MS-MQ*`).\n\nWhen a user asks a broad question, start from family prefixes and narrow to specific protocol IDs.\n\n## When to Use / When Not to Use\n\nUse this skill when the user asks for:\n\n- Protocol semantics, message flow, field definitions, or sequencing rules.\n- Cross-reference analysis between related specs.\n- Security semantics and product-behavior distinctions in Open Specifications docs.\n\nDo not use this skill as the primary source for:\n\n- API usage tutorials, SDK how-to steps, or implementation quickstarts.\n- Product configuration guidance not grounded in protocol specs.\n\nIf a required protocol is missing from root-level `MS-*` directories, state that explicitly and ask the user for the exact protocol ID or a narrower feature scope.\n\n## Navigation Strategy\n\n- **Domain/topic questions** (file access, authentication, storage, remote desktop, etc.): Start with the corresponding Overview document from README. Use it as a map to identify which specifications to read. Follow its links into those specs.\n- **Protocol-ID questions**: Go directly to the spec if the ID is known.\n- **Principle**: Overview documents are the primary entry point for topical discovery. README provides the index of Overview docs and the full protocol list, but does not contain the semantic mapping (topic → protocols) found in Overviews.\n- **Anti-pattern**: Do not rely on README keyword search alone. A shallow grep of README may return protocol IDs from unrelated domains; overview documents provide the curated topic-to-protocol mapping.\n\n## Navigation Workflow\n\n1. For topical questions: Identify the domain from the question, match to an Overview document in README, read it to obtain linked member specs, then follow links into those specs.\n2. For known protocol IDs: Validate in `README.md` and directory names (`<PROTOCOL-ID>/`), then open the spec.\n3. Start from the spec TOC (`<summary>` blocks and numbered entries) before deep reading.\n4. Read sections in this order by intent: orientation/versioning, message or structure syntax, behavior and sequencing, security and product behavior notes.\n5. Cross-check base vs extension specs when requirements may be split.\n6. Answer with explicit protocol IDs and exact section headings; separate confirmed facts from inference.\n\n## Link-Following\n\n- Overview documents contain References sections (often 1.3) and extensive inline links to member specifications. Follow these links rather than guessing paths.\n- The link graph (Overview → spec → related spec) is the intended navigation structure.\n- When a spec references another spec for types, extensions, or dependencies, follow that link to reach the authoritative source.\n- Continue following links until the relevant information is found; do not stop at the first document that mentions the topic.\n\n## Canonical Spec Structure (Corpus-Guided)\n\nThe corpus is highly consistent. The most common top-level sequence is:\n\n- `1 Introduction`\n- `2 Messages`\n- `3 Protocol Details`\n- `4 Protocol Examples`\n- `5 Security`\n\nCommon `1.x` orientation subsections include:\n\n- `1.1 Glossary`, `1.2 References`, `1.3 Overview`\n- `1.4 Relationship to Other Protocols`\n- `1.5 Prerequisites/Preconditions`\n- `1.7 Versioning and Capability Negotiation`\n\nCommon `3.x.y` behavioral subsections include:\n\n- `Abstract Data Model`\n- `Timers`\n- `Initialization`\n- `Higher-Layer Triggered Events`\n- `Message Processing Events and Sequencing Rules`\n- `Timer Events`\n- `Other Local Events`\n\nUse these sections as the default reading spine unless the document is an outlier.\n\n## Section-First Reading Playbook\n\nPrioritize sections by question type:\n\n- “What is this protocol / where does it fit?” -> `1.3`, `1.4`, `1.7`\n- “How is data encoded / what are fields?” -> `2.2` (`Message Syntax`, `Common Data Types`, structures)\n- “What is the runtime behavior / state machine?” -> `3.x` details and `3.x.y` sequencing sections\n- “What security guarantees or knobs exist?” -> `5.*` security sections\n- “Implementation differences by product/version?” -> `Appendix ... Product Behavior` and change tracking sections\n\nWhen structure spans multiple specs, resolve in this order:\n\n1. Base/core protocol semantics.\n2. Extension-specific modifications.\n3. Shared type dependencies (for example `MS-DTYP`).\n\n## Outlier Handling\n\nNot all specs use the exact canonical headings. Handle these common variants:\n\n- `2 Structures`, `2 Attributes`, `2 Data Types`, `2 Message Transport` instead of `2 Messages`.\n- `3 Structure Examples`, `3 Details`, or algorithm-specific section names.\n- `4 Security` or `4 Security Considerations` when numbering shifts.\n- Appendix variants such as `Full IDL`, `Full WSDL`, `Full XML Schema`, `Full JSON Schema`.\n- Change tracking may appear as section `7`, `8`, `9`, or higher.\n\nRule: match by semantic intent first, section number second.\n\n## Quick Discovery Patterns\n\n- When the protocol ID is unknown: Identify the domain first from question keywords, then open the matching Overview document before picking specs. Use its Protocol Summary or References section to obtain the correct spec list.\n- Do not select specs from README''s flat Technical Documents list without consulting an Overview when the domain is ambiguous.\n- When the user provides a specific protocol ID: Go directly to that spec.\n- For extension behavior: Verify whether requirements are in a base protocol or an extension; Overview docs and spec cross-references help clarify dependencies.\n- For ambiguous acronyms: List 2–4 likely protocols (via Overview docs) and ask the user to choose before deep analysis.\n\n## Answer Contract (Semi-Structured)\n\nDefault answer shape:\n\n1. `Protocols consulted`: list exact IDs.\n2. `Sections used`: list exact section titles (and numbers when available).\n3. `Findings`: concise facts tied to those sections.\n4. `Inference / uncertainty`: explicit separation from confirmed text.\n\nEvidence policy:\n\n- For non-obvious, contested, or security-sensitive claims, include section-grounded evidence.\n- For straightforward facts, concise section references are enough.\n- If two specs disagree, report both and identify likely version/context scope.\n\n## Working Style\n\n- Prefer section-grounded answers over high-level paraphrase.\n- Include the exact protocol IDs used for the answer.\n- If the corpus does not clearly answer a point, state uncertainty explicitly.\n- Never present inferred behavior as normative requirement text.\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:13:34.493Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Analysis Agents requiring in-depth knowledge of Microsoft Open Specifications and Windows Protocols.","zh":"适合需要对 Microsoft Open Specifications 和 Windows Protocols 有深入了解的技术分析代理","ja":"Microsoft Open Specifications と Windows Protocols に関する深い知識が必要なテクニカル分析エージェントに適しています","ko":"Microsoft Open Specifications 및 Windows Protocols에 대한 심도 있는 지식을 요구하는 기술 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Análisis Técnico que requieren conocimientos profundos de las Especificaciones Abiertas de Microsoft y los Protocolos de Windows.","fr":"Idéal pour les Agents d''Analyse Technique nécessitant une connaissance approfondie des Spécifications Ouvertes de Microsoft et des Protocoles Windows.","de":"Ideal für technische Analyseagenten, die umfassende Kenntnisse der Microsoft Open Specifications und der Windows-Protokolle erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise Técnica que exigem conhecimento aprofundado das Especificações Abertas da Microsoft e Protocolos do Windows.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов технического анализа, требующих глубоких знаний открытых спецификаций Microsoft и протоколов Windows.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التحليل الفني الذي يتطلب معرفة متعمقة بمواصفات مايكروسوفت المفتوحة وبروتوكولات ويندوز."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate Microsoft Open Specifications markdown and provide evidence-grounded answers regarding Windows Protocols, leveraging local file analysis and structure-first navigation, with support for domain maps and technical documents in markdown format.","zh":"赋予代理导航 Microsoft Open Specifications markdown 并提供有关 Windows Protocols 的证据基础答案的能力，利用本地文件分析和结构优先导航，并支持 markdown 格式的域图和技术文档","ja":"Microsoft Open Specifications の markdown をナビゲートし、Windows Protocols に関する証拠に基づいた回答を提供するエージェントをエンパワーメントします。ローカルファイル分析と構造優先ナビゲーションを利用し、markdown 形式のドメインマップと技術文書をサポートします","ko":"Microsoft Open Specifications markdown를 탐색하고 Windows Protocols에 대한 근거 기반 답변을 제공하는 에이전트를 강화합니다. 로컬 파일 분석과 구조 우선 탐색을 활용하며, markdown 형식의 도메인 맵 및 기술 문서를 지원합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a navegar por la documentación de Especificaciones Abiertas de Microsoft en markdown y proporcionar respuestas basadas en evidencia sobre los Protocolos de Windows, aprovechando el análisis de archivos locales y la navegación estructura-primero, con soporte para mapas de dominio y documentos técnicos en formato markdown.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer dans la documentation des Spécifications Ouvertes de Microsoft en markdown et de fournir des réponses fondées sur des preuves concernant les Protocoles Windows, en exploitant l''analyse de fichiers locaux et la navigation structure-première, avec un support pour les cartes de domaine et les documents techniques au format markdown.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, die Microsoft Open Specifications-Dokumentation in Markdown zu navigieren und evidenzbasierte Antworten zu den Windows-Protokollen zu liefern, indem sie die lokale Dateianalyse und die strukturorientierte Navigation nutzen, mit Unterstützung für Domänenkarten und technische Dokumente im Markdown-Format.","pt":"Permite que os agentes naveguem pelas especificações markdown da Microsoft Open e forneçam respostas baseadas em evidências sobre os Protocolos do Windows, aproveitando a análise de arquivos locais e navegação estruturada primeiro, com suporte a mapas de domínio e documentos técnicos no formato markdown.","ru":"Позволяет агентам ориентироваться в документации открытых спецификаций Microsoft в формате markdown и предоставлять ответы, основанные на доказательствах, касающихся протоколов Windows, используя анализ локальных файлов и структуру первой навигации, с поддержкой карт доменов и технической документации в формате markdown.","ar":"تمكن العميل من التنقل في مواصفات مايكروسوفت المفتوحة بالتنسيق markdown وتقديم إجابات مدعومة بالأدلة حول بروتوكولات ويندوز، مستفيدا من تحليل الملفات المحلية والتنقل الهيكلي الأول، مع دعم خرائط النطاق والوثائق الفنية بتنسيق markdown."},"useCases":{"en":["Navigating Windows Protocols documentation","Providing evidence-grounded answers on Microsoft Open Specifications","Analyzing technical documents for Windows development"],"zh":["导航 Windows Protocols 文档","提供有关 Microsoft Open Specifications 的证据基础答案","分析 Windows 开发的技术文档"],"ja":["Windows Protocols ドキュメントのナビゲート","Microsoft Open Specifications に関する証拠に基づいた回答を提供","Windows 開発の技術文書の分析"],"ko":["Windows Protocols 문서 탐색","Microsoft Open Specifications에 대한 근거 기반 답변 제공","Windows 개발을 위한 기술 문서 분석"],"es":["Navegar por la documentación de Protocolos de Windows","Proporcionar respuestas basadas en evidencia sobre las Especificaciones Abiertas de Microsoft","Analizar documentos técnicos para el desarrollo de Windows"],"fr":["Naviguer dans la documentation des Protocoles Windows","Fournir des réponses fondées sur des preuves concernant les Spécifications Ouvertes de Microsoft","Analyser des documents techniques pour le développement de Windows"],"de":["Durch die Windows-Protokolle-Dokumentation navigieren","Evidenzbasierte Antworten zu den Microsoft Open Specifications liefern","Technische Dokumente für die Windows-Entwicklung analysieren"],"pt":["Navegando pela documentação dos Protocolos do Windows","Fornecendo respostas baseadas em evidências sobre as Especificações Abertas da Microsoft","Analysando documentos técnicos para desenvolvimento do Windows"],"ru":["Ориентирование в документации протоколов Windows","Предоставление ответов, основанных на доказательствах, об открытых спецификациях Microsoft","Анализ технической документации для разработки Windows"],"ar":["التنقل في وثائق بروتوكولات ويندوز","تقديم إجابات مدعومة بالأدلة حول مواصفات مايكروسوفت المفتوحة","تحليل الوثائق الفنية لتنمية ويندوز"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires local access to markdown corpus","Does not support network lookup","Limited to Microsoft Open Specifications Windows Protocols"],"zh":["需要访问本地 markdown 语料库","不支持网络查找","仅限 Microsoft Open Specifications Windows Protocols"],"ja":["ローカル markdown コーパスへのアクセスが必要","ネットワーク検索はサポートされていません","Microsoft Open Specifications Windows Protocols 限定"],"ko":["로컬 markdown 코퍼스에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","네트워크 조회를 지원하지 않습니다","Microsoft Open Specifications Windows Protocols만 해당"],"es":["Requiere acceso local al corpus de markdown","No admite la búsqueda en red","Limitado a las Especificaciones Abiertas de Microsoft y los Protocolos de Windows"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès local au corpus de markdown","Ne prend pas en charge la recherche en réseau","Limité aux Spécifications Ouvertes de Microsoft et aux Protocoles Windows"],"de":["Benötigt lokalen Zugriff auf das Markdown-Corpus","Unterstützt keine Netzwerksuche","Begrenzt auf die Microsoft Open Specifications und die Windows-Protokolle"],"pt":["Exige acesso local ao corpus markdown","Não suporta pesquisa de rede","Limitado às Especificações Abertas da Microsoft e 